{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011CdosneWAnSHxeg8qDDaCK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A few key dimensions to weigh:\n\n**Migration cost**\n- How much historical data matters (closed issues, links, attachments, custom fields)?\n- Does the new tracker have an import tool, or is it manual/scripted?\n\n**Workflow fit**\n- Does it match how your team actually works (kanban vs. scrum vs. ad-hoc)?\n- Custom fields, automation rules, and recurring workflows — are they expressible in the new system?\n\n**Integration surface**\n- Git/PR linking, CI/CD, Slack/comms, time tracking — what breaks on day one?\n- API quality if you have internal tooling that reads/writes issues.\n\n**Team adoption friction**\n- How opinionated is the new tool vs. your current one? Simpler tools often win on adoption even if they're less powerful.\n- Who are the power users most at risk of revolting?\n\n**Cost at your scale**\n- Per-seat pricing vs. flat tiers matters a lot depending on team size and growth trajectory.\n\n**Lock-in**\n- Can you export everything in a portable format later? Proprietary data models are the main regret people cite after switching.\n\nThe most common mistake is optimizing for features the team rarely uses while underweighting the migration disruption cost and the 2–3 months of reduced velocity during the transition. If you share what tracker you're on now and what's driving the switch, I can give more targeted advice."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7822,"cache_read_input_tokens":19604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7822},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17017461-e11c-4c03-a0cb-ec3e40cc2e7e","uuid":"61be6a6a-311d-4a3c-a73a-929b9d686bd